een**, and the rocky riverbanks and boulders are now clearly visible without atmospheric haze. The lighting is harsh and direct, creating crisp shadows and reflecting off the water's surface.\n\n**Frames 367s through 374s remain static** (or near-identical), maintaining this sunny daytime view without camera movement or action. The river flows gently through the valley, bordered by dense green forest and large rock formations. No people, animals, or man-made objects are visible, and there is no text overlay. The mood shifts from ethereal and contemplative to bright and matter-of-fact, emphasizing the same geographical location under vastly different seasonal or temporal conditions.", 'similarity score': 0.5011794567108154}, {'clip_0_6': 'clip_0_6', 'text': 'This sequence is a title card intro for "**Geography King**."\n\n**0.0s–1.0s:** The clip opens with an extreme close-up of blurry, large serif text against a bright, lens-flared background with green and blue gradient hues; only fragments like "rap" are partially visible.\n\n**1.0s–2.0s:** The camera pulls back slightly, revealing the partial text "**ography K**" superimposed over a stylized world map showing Africa and surrounding oceans in green and blue.\n\n**2.0s–5.0s:** The view zooms out to reveal a complete, centered globe displaying the Eastern Hemisphere (Europe, Africa, Asia, Australia). The full title "**Geography King**" appears in large, brown serif letters with white outlines across the center. The background features a soft blue-to-green radial gradient with a bright light flare in the upper-left corner.\n\n**5.0s–6.0s:** The image holds steady before gradually dimming, with the entire frame fading to a darker, muted version while the title and globe remain visible.\n\n**Overall:** No people appear; the focus is on the graphical globe and title reveal. The mood is educational and grandiose, typical of an introductory sequence for a geography-themed video or channel, using lens flares and dramatic zoom-outs to create a sense of scale.', 'similarity score': 0.5003460645675659}, {'clip_168_173': 'clip_168_173', 'text': 'The sequence transitions from a lively summer beach scene to a static aerial cityscape.\n\n**Frame 168s (Odesa):** A crowded, sunlit beach teems with activity. Dozens of people in swimwear sunbathe on towels and lounge chairs, while others wade in the surf or walk along the shore. A jet ski sits near the water\'s edge, and a yellow inflatable banana boat lies on the sand. The atmosphere is energetic and recreational, typical of peak summer tourism. The text "Odesa" appears in yellow at the bottom.\n\n**Frames 169s–173s (Dnipro):** The scene shifts to a static, wide aerial view of an urban waterfront under an overcast, grayish sky. The camera overlooks the city of Dnipro, showing a mix of modern high-rises and older, lower-rise buildings along the wide Dnieper River. A bridge spans the river on the left, while tree-lined embankments show autumn foliage. The streets below have sparse traffic. The mood is calm, cooler, and distinctly urban compared to the previous beach setting. The text "Dnipro" remains fixed at the bottom throughout these frames, which appear nearly identical with no discernible movement.', 'similarity score': 0.49136531352996826}, {'clip_202_212': 'clip_202_212', 'text': 'The sequence begins with two frames (202s–203s) displaying a static data table titled **"Largest cities or towns in Ukraine"** dated 2021-12-31. The table lists major Ukrainian cities (Kyiv, Kharkiv, Odesa, Dnipro, Donetsk, Lviv, etc.) with their respective regions and populations, presented in a clean, Wikipedia-style format.\n\nAt 204s, the video cuts abruptly to a starkly different scene held for the remaining frames through 212s. This shows the **aftermath of destruction** at a Soviet-era apartment complex. A multi-story concrete residential building exhibits severe war damage: blown-out windows, destroyed balconies, charred exterior walls, and debris scattered across the muddy ground. In the foreground, a young person stands holding a bicycle, staring up at the damaged structure. Several residents gather in small groups near the entrance and beside a damaged white car, while others appear on a partially destroyed balcony. Two dogs wander near the building, and leafless trees suggest a cold, late autumn or winter setting. The lighting is overcast and gray, contributing to a somber, bleak mood that contrasts sharply with the clinical statistics of the opening frames, humanizing the data with visible devastation.', 'similarity score': 0.4907977283000946}, {'clip_271_276': 'clip_271_276', 'text': '**Frame 271s:** The video opens on a close-up of a large turbofan jet engine displayed indoors, likely at an exhibition or trade show. The engine sits on white support stands against a blue backdrop featuring a white stylized wing-like logo. The exposed internal components show green-colored fan blades and intricate silver piping and mechanics. The setting includes red carpet flooring and overhead lighting, suggesting a professional showcase environment.\n\n**Frames 272s–276s:** The scene transitions to a static exterior shot of an industrial oil refinery or petrochemical plant held for the remaining five seconds. The facility features tall, weathered metal distillation towers with external piping and scaffolding, connected by an elevated walkway or conveyor bridge that spans across a paved access road. Blue storage tanks and additional industrial infrastructure are visible beneath a bright blue sky with scattered white clouds. No personnel or movement is visible in the facility, creating a still, documentary-style atmosphere. The persistent static shot suggests this serves as establishing imagery while narration continues. \n\nThe sequence connects advanced aerospace manufacturing (the precision engine) with heavy industrial infrastructure (the refinery), emphasizing technological and industrial capabilities. No readable text appears in any frame.', 'similarity score': 0.4897438883781433}, {'clip_138_144': 'clip_138_144', 'text': "This video segment transitions from a linguistic map to an aerial cityscape:\n\n**Frames 138s–139s:** A static map displays the geographical distribution of Ukrainian dialects across Ukraine and neighboring regions (Poland, Belarus, Russia, Romania). The map uses color-coded regions (red, blue, yellow, and patterned areas) with numbered labels (1–17) corresponding to a legend in the bottom-left corner identifying specific dialect groups. Major cities like Kyiv, Lviv, Kharkiv, and Odesa are marked, along with the Black Sea and Sea of Azov.\n\n**Frames 140s–144s:** The scene cuts to a static aerial view of **Kyiv** (labeled in yellow text at the bottom). The shot centers on **St. Sophia's Cathedral** with its distinctive green roofs and golden domes, accompanied by its tall white bell tower with a golden cupola. The view captures a large open plaza adjacent to the cathedral, surrounded by trees, historic buildings, and the dense urban grid of the capital city under bright daylight.\n\n**Mood:** The sequence shifts from an academic, informative tone (linguistic analysis) to a scenic, visually appealing presentation of Ukrainian cultural heritage and urban landscape.", 'similarity score': 0.48371562361717224}, {'clip_374_383': 'clip_374_383', 'text': 'The video transitions between two distinct, static landscape shots:\n\n**374s–375s:** The sequence opens with a wide, elevated view of a rocky river valley under a bright blue sky with scattered white clouds. A river winds through arid, brush-covered terrain dotted with large boulders and rocky outcrops, while green vegetation lines the banks. The scene is sunlit and expansive, suggesting a dry, rugged environment.\n\n**376s–383s:** At approximately 376s, the scene cuts to a serene, misty countryside. A single, vibrant green tree stands prominently on rolling grassy hills, backlit by soft morning light. Behind it, layers of forested mountains fade into fog, with a rustic wooden fence running along the hillside. The atmosphere shifts dramatically to damp, tranquil, and ethereal with muted, pastel tones.\n\n**Details:** No people, animals, or text appear in any frame. The camera remains static throughout both segments, creating a contemplative, peaceful mood emphasizing natural beauty and stillness. The transition marks a shift from arid, rocky openness to lush, misty intimacy.', 'similarity score': 0.47614169120788574}, {'clip_144_150': 'clip_144_150', 'text': '**Frame 144s:** An aerial establishing shot captures a sunlit panoramic view of Kyiv, prominently featuring the golden-domed St. Michael\'s Golden-Domed Monastery and bell tower surrounded by lush greenery and dense urban architecture. A large Ukrainian flag is visible spread across grounds near the cathedral. The text "Kyiv" appears at the bottom.\n\n**Frames 145–150s:** The scene cuts to a ground-level wide shot of Maidan Nezalezhnosti (Independence Square) packed with thousands of people, suggesting a major protest or rally. The crowd fills the vast plaza bordered by classical Soviet-era buildings. Dominating the right side is a massive billboard bearing the patriotic Ukrainian text **"СЛАВА УКРАЇНІ! ГЕРОЯМ СЛАВА!"** (Glory to Ukraine! Glory to the Heroes!) decorated with floral motifs. The camera remains static on this dense, energetic crowd for the duration of the sequence. The text "Kyiv" persists at the bottom of the frame.\n\n**Overall:** The sequence transitions from a serene, scenic overview of Kyiv\'s historic architecture to an intense, civic atmosphere of mass public assembly, conveying a mood of national pride and collective political engagement.', 'similarity score': 0.4729602634906769}, {'clip_52_60': 'clip_52_60', 'text': 'The sequence transitions between two static informational graphics with no visible movement or characters:\n\n**Frames 52s–53s:** A political map of Eastern Europe and the Black Sea region is displayed. Ukraine is highlighted in purple, surrounded by labeled neighboring countries including Poland, Belarus, Slovakia, Hungary, Romania, Moldova, Serbia, Bulgaria, Greece, and Turkey. The Black Sea is visible to the southeast.\n\n**Frames 54s–60s:** The view switches to a vertical bar chart titled "Composition of Ukraine by ethnicity," citing the 2001 Census. The chart displays ethnic breakdowns: Ukrainians (77.8%), Russians (17.3%), Romanians and Moldovans (0.8%), Belarusians (0.6%), Crimean Tatars (0.5%), Bulgarians (0.4%), Hungarians (0.3%), Poles (0.3%), and Others (1.7%). A source citation at the bottom reads: "Ethnic composition of the population of Ukraine, 2001 Census."\n\n**Setting/Mood:** The setting is purely graphical/data visualization with a neutral, educational documentary tone, presenting geographic and demographic facts without narrative commentary or human presence.', 'similarity score': 0.472952663898468}, {'clip_326_334': 'clip_326_334', 'text': 'The sequence opens with a sweeping panoramic view (326s) of a lush, mountainous valley dotted with scattered rural homes and patches of forest, with a prominent peak rising in the background under clear blue skies. \n\nThe scene then transitions at 327s to a static, ground-level shot of a grassy mountain summit that remains unchanged through the end of the sequence (334s). The foreground shows rocky, alpine terrain with scattered stones, while the background features a steep, verdant peak against a bright blue sky with sparse white clouds. Yellow text at the bottom of the frame identifies the mountain as **"Mt. Hoverla (2,061 m)"**—indicating this is the highest peak in the Ukrainian Carpathians.\n\nThe mood is serene and majestic, emphasizing the natural beauty and scale of the mountain landscape with no visible human activity or movement.', 'similarity score': 0.4691222906112671}, {'clip_155_163': 'clip_155_163', 'text': 'The sequence opens with an aerial establishing shot of **Kharkiv** (155s), displaying a sprawling inland cityscape of mid-rise and high-rise buildings under a pale, partly cloudy sky. A distinctive red-roofed building with white trim and a small tower stands out among the urban density.\n\nAt 156s, the scene cuts to a static aerial view of **Odesa**, which remains held through the end of the sequence (163s). This coastal cityscape features a bustling port with docks and piers extending into calm blue waters, a curved sandy beachfront, and a densely built urban area climbing inland from the shoreline. The architecture consists primarily of white and beige residential towers interspersed with greenery, while a hazy, overcast sky softens the horizon.\n\n**Visible text:** Yellow labels identify each city—"Kharkiv" in the first frame and "Odesa" in all subsequent frames.\n\n**Mood:** The tone is documentary and observational, presenting these locations as calm, living cities without visible human activity or movement—serving as geographic context or establishing shots.', 'similarity score': 0.4688815176486969}, {'clip_194_202': 'clip_194_202', 'text': 'The video opens with a bright, sunlit aerial view of **Lviv**, Ukraine (labeled at the bottom of the frame), showcasing a prominent white baroque church with green roofing and a tall tower, surrounded by dense trees and historic buildings with terracotta and grey rooftops. This picturesque urban landscape occupies the first frame (~194s) before cutting to a static data visualization for the remainder of the sequence (195s–202s). \n\nThe subsequent frames display a table titled **"Largest cities or towns in Ukraine"** (dated 2021-12-31) against a black background. The chart lists cities by rank, showing **Kyiv** (2,962,180) at the top, followed by **Kharkiv** (1,433,886), **Odesa** (1,015,826), **Dnipro** (1,046,302), **Donetsk** (905,364), **Zaporizhzhia** (710,052), **Lviv** (721,510), and others down to **Cherkasy** (272,851), with columns for Rank, Name, Region, and Population. \n\n**Mood and context:** The sequence shifts from an inviting, scenic geographic introduction to a clinical, statistical presentation, providing demographic context for Ukrainian urban centers without any visible human action or camera movement during the table display.', 'similarity score': 0.4682236313819885}, {'clip_212_221': 'clip_212_221', 'text': 'The sequence presents a stark tonal and visual shift between two distinct environments:\n\n**Frame at 212s:** The video opens on a bleak, post-conflict urban scene. A damaged, grey Soviet-era apartment building dominates the background, with blown-out windows, destroyed balconies, and charred exterior walls. In the foreground, a young person stands with a teal bicycle facing the building, while several residents gather in small groups across the debris-strewn, muddy grounds. Two dogs wander near the center. Leafless trees and overcast lighting contribute to a somber, desolate atmosphere suggesting recent destruction or shelling.\n\n**Frames 213s–221s:** The scene abruptly cuts to a static, idyllic rural setting that holds for the remaining duration. A traditional wooden hut with a steep thatched roof sits amid lush greenery, enclosed by a rustic woven fence. Vibrant red poppies bloom in the tall grass foreground. A person in traditional dress stands near the fence beside the weathered wooden structure. Bright sunlight, verdant trees, and vibrant wildflowers create a peaceful, nostalgic mood—standing in sharp contrast to the preceding urban devastation. No visible text appears in any frame.', 'similarity score': 0.46692955493927}, {'clip_221_229': 'clip_221_229', 'text': '**Setting & Environment**  \nThe sequence opens with a wide establishing shot (221s) of a traditional log cabin with a steep thatched roof, surrounded by lush greenery and red poppies blooming along a rustic wooden fence. The setting appears to be a preserved historical village or rural homestead, with dirt paths and mature trees suggesting late spring or summer.\n\n**Subject & Action**  \nAt 222s, the scene cuts to a static medium shot of an elderly woman leaning on a rough-hewn wooden fence, which holds for the remainder of the sequence (222s–229s). She wears a patterned white headscarf and a dark, modest coat. Her hands are clasped calmly on the fence rail as she gazes slightly off-camera with a gentle, contemplative expression. She remains motionless throughout, creating a portrait-like stillness.\n\n**Visual Details**  \nBehind her stands another traditional cottage with clay-plastered walls and a thick thatched roof featuring a distinctive stepped ridge and small chimney structure. The lighting shifts from bright sunlight in the opening wide shot to softer, diffused daylight in the portrait.\n\n**Mood**  \nThe atmosphere is serene, nostalgic, and timeless—evoking a sense of rootedness in traditional rural life and quiet resilience. No text or dialogue is visible in any frame.', 'similarity score': 0.46667131781578064}, {'clip_180_188': 'clip_180_188', 'text': 'The sequence presents a stark temporal contrast of Donetsk, transitioning from a winter evening to a spring daytime setting.\n\n**Frame at 180s:** A panoramic aerial view captures Donetsk at dusk or dawn during winter. Snow blankets the rooftops of high-rise residential buildings and streets, while warm streetlights glow against the cold blue and orange hues of the sky. The city appears quiet and serene under the snow cover.\n\n**Frames 181s–188s:** The scene cuts to an identical vantage point in warmer months, holding a static daytime shot for the remaining duration. The snow has melted, revealing green parks with pathways, leafy trees, and the same residential architecture. In the background, modern glass skyscrapers—including a distinctive curved blue tower and a beige building with a green dome-contrast with older Soviet-era apartment blocks. A yellow piece of construction equipment is visible on one of the streets below.\n\n**Text and Mood:** The word "Donetsk" appears in yellow text at the bottom of all frames. The sequence shifts from a contemplative, cold winter twilight to a brighter, calmer spring atmosphere, emphasizing the passage of time and seasonal change in the urban landscape. No human activity is visible; the focus remains entirely on the architectural and environmental setting.', 'similarity score': 0.46553611755371094}, {'clip_305_314': 'clip_305_314', 'text': '**0:305–0:306:** A hand holds a clear plastic bottle of golden sunflower oil against a lush sunflower field backdrop, emphasizing the natural source of the product. The background shows blooming yellow sunflowers and green foliage in soft focus.\n\n**0:307–0:314:** The scene transitions to a clean white background displaying a product lineup of five different container sizes of "Диканька" (Dikanka) sunflower oil, ranging from small bottles to large 5-liter jugs. All containers feature green labels with sunflower imagery and the brand name in Cyrillic text. The shot remains static, showcasing the packaging variety.\n\n**Overall:** The sequence moves from an organic, outdoor lifestyle shot to a straightforward commercial product display, highlighting both the natural origins and available retail formats of the cooking oil.', 'similarity score': 0.46290165185928345}]
Caption search results: [{'clip_383_410': 'clip_383_410', 'text': 'The sequence opens with a brief scenic shot at 383s showing a lone, lush green tree standing on a rolling hillside with misty mountains in the background, creating a serene, pastoral mood.\n\nAt 384s, the video cuts to a medium close-up of a man speaking directly to the camera, which continues through the end of the segment at 409s. The speaker, a man with short brown hair and light stubble wearing a cream-colored button-down shirt, is positioned in what appears to be a home office or study. Behind him, the wall is decorated with: a large vintage-style world map (appearing to show both hemispheres), a wooden silhouette of California, a decorative metal lizard figure, a license plate reading "**375 KEB**," a wooden paddle or oar, and various small photos or postcards pinned to the wall.\n\nThroughout the duration (384s–409s), the man maintains direct eye contact with the camera while speaking, his expression and mouth movements shifting as he articulates points—occasionally appearing thoughtful or slightly concerned, then resuming a conversational tone. The camera remains static, focusing on him from the chest up, maintaining consistent lighting and framing throughout his monologue. The overall mood is informative and personal, typical of a vlog or educational video format.', 'similarity score': 0.7310415506362915}, {'clip_37_46': 'clip_37_46', 'text': 'The sequence begins with a medium close-up of a man in a cream-colored button-down shirt speaking directly to the camera (37s–38s). He has short dark hair and facial stubble, and his expression shifts slightly as he talks. The background features a vintage-style world map, a wooden California state outline, a decorative metal lizard, a license plate reading "375 KEB," and a wooden paddle mounted on a muted green wall.\n\nAt approximately 38s, the scene transitions to a static political map of Europe (39s–46s). The map displays modern country boundaries with distinct color-coding (e.g., France in pink, Italy in yellow, Russia in pale yellow, Spain in mint green). Country names and major bodies of water (Atlantic Ocean, Black Sea) are labeled in black text. The watermark "MAPSWIRE" appears in the bottom-right corner. The map remains unchanged throughout the remainder of the sequence, suggesting an educational or explanatory context.', 'similarity score': 0.6475896239280701}, {'clip_6_37': 'clip_6_37', 'text': '**Sequence Overview:**\n\nThe video opens with a title card (6s) displaying the text **"Geography King"** in serif font overlaid on a spinning globe against a green-blue gradient background. \n\nAt 8s, the scene transitions to a medium close-up of a man speaking directly to camera. He appears to be in his 40s-50s with short dark hair, a beard, and wearing a light-colored button-down shirt. The setting is a room decorated with geography/travel-themed items: behind him hangs a large multi-panel antique-style world map, a wooden canoe paddle, a wooden cutout of California, a colorful decorative lizard, and a license plate reading **"375 KEB"** (visible throughout).\n\nFrom 8s to 35s, the man continues talking with varying facial expressions—opening his mouth wide, raising eyebrows, squinting slightly, and showing subtle emotional shifts that suggest he\'s explaining or emphasizing points. The camera remains static, focused on him from the chest up, with the background unchanged. \n\n**Mood:** Educational and conversational, typical of an instructional video or vlog format. The consistent eye contact and changing expressions indicate an engaging, direct-to-audience presentation style.', 'similarity score': 0.6361111402511597}, {'clip_410_422': 'clip_410_422', 'text': 'The sequence opens with a medium shot of a man in a cream-colored button-down shirt seated in a personal office or study (410s). Behind him, the wall displays eclectic decor: a multi-panel world map, a wooden California state silhouette, a decorative paddle, a license plate reading "375 KEB," and a colorful gecko decal.\n\nAt 411s, the video cuts to a static photograph that remains unchanged through 422s. The image depicts two shirtless heavyweight boxers—the Klitschko brothers (Wladimir and Vitali)—posing together in a gym setting. Both wear bright red boxing gloves (branded "LANGSDORF" on the left fighter and "TWINS" on the right). The boxer on the left drapes his right arm over the other\'s shoulder while both face the camera with serious expressions. The background shows gym equipment and a partially visible sign reading "DeRo" on the wall.\n\nThe mood transitions from intimate and conversational (the speaker\'s workspace) to athletic and nostalgic (the vintage boxing portrait), suggesting a documentary or biographical segment discussing the fighters\' careers.', 'similarity score': 0.6321330666542053}, {'clip_105_111': 'clip_105_111', 'text': 'The sequence opens with two frames (105s–106s) depicting the interior of the Ukrainian Parliament (Verkhovna Rada) in session. The grand chamber features a semi-circular arrangement of wooden desks with red upholstered seating, occupied by numerous parliamentarians—most seated and working, while others stand and move about. Classical white columns, ornate balconies, and a large Ukrainian flag behind the central speaker’s podium dominate the architecture. The atmosphere is formal, institutional, and active with legislative business.\n\nAt 107s, the scene cuts to an outdoor winter protest that remains static for the subsequent five frames (107s–111s). Set in an urban environment with tall, stately white buildings and leafless trees, the focus is on a protester photographed from behind, wearing a dark winter jacket with "**UKRAINE**" printed across the back. The individual holds a large Ukrainian flag (horizontal blue over yellow) high overhead with both gloved hands. Surrounding demonstrators wave additional Ukrainian flags, with some Canadian flags visible in the cro